WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.120
- What the heck is ketogenic diet?

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.090
- [Narrator] Quickly lose weight.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.250
- Fats with benefits.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.340
- Satiates your appetite.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.380
- She chose this.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.213
- He chose this.

00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:08.410
- [Reporter] Butter is good.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.630
- Explain yourself.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.020
- The ketogenic diet,

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.680
let's break down what
all this hype is about.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.280
I'm gonna tell you what it is,

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.780
briefly how it works,

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.190
and discuss some of the claims

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.050
they're most commonly made on the subject.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:21.951
Let's get started.

00:00:21.951 --> 00:00:24.534
(upbeat music)

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.540
Before we get into the ketogenic diet,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.590
let's break down some very
simple nutrition basics.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.810
There're three major macronutrient groups

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.670
that we're gonna be paying attention to:

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.350
proteins, fats, and carbs.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.520
These are nutrients that you
find in the foods you eat

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.570
every single day.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:45.610
This standard American diet
consists of 35% of fats,

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.390
15% of proteins, and 50% of carbs.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.240
Now if you're looking at ketogenic diet,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.862
the numbers are quite
different with 75% being fats,

00:00:54.862 --> 00:00:59.360
20% being proteins, and
only 5% being carbs.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.590
Think about that, that's
10 times less carbs

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.290
than in an standard American diet.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.590
Let's say you switch
from your standard diet

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.600
to a ketogenic diet, what
happens inside of your body?

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.540
Your body deals with this
very low carb consumption

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.570
in two ways: first, it enters
a state called ketosis,

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.760
which shifts your body's energy
source to a primarily fats.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.160
Which basically means
that it breaks down fats

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.040
into something known as
ketones, hence ketosis,

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.940
and then uses those for energy.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.740
Simply put, your body begins to burn fat

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.210
as its primary energy source,
and moves away from glucose,

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.310
which is a carbohydrate.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:40.880
The process of going into
ketosis does take a few days,

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.020
and during those days,

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.460
people experience some
adverse side effects:

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.920
brain fog, irritability,
nausea, GI discomfort.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.250
Some people label this the "Keto Flu."

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.020
- I don't feel so good.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.580
- The second process your
body uses is gluconeogenesis,

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.520
which sounds scary, but it's really not.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.410
All it is is your body creating glucose

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:03.030
because now all cells can
function on fats alone.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.750
Fun fact here, for survival purposes,

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.210
you don't need to consume any carbs

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.760
as long as you're getting
enough fats and proteins.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:14.970
Now where did all of this hype

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:17.230
for the ketogenic diet come from?

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.923
Let's take a look at the claims
and find out what's true,

00:02:19.923 --> 00:02:21.040
and what's not.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.110
Claim number one,

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.590
the ketogenic diet is
good for weight loss.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:27.420
Yeah, the ketogenic diet
is good for weight loss,

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.310
and this happens through
two important mechanisms.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.060
First, since you're using fats

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.770
as your primary energy source,

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.690
you're burning a lot of stored fat.

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:40.110
Second, because fat is very
satiating, makes you feel full,

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.740
when you eat a high fat content meal,

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.530
you actually don't want to eat as much.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.810
Therefore, you limit the
amount of calories you take in

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.643
throughout the day.

00:02:47.643 --> 00:02:49.060
A lot of people are surprised that

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.850
when they start the ketogenic
diet, that they lose weight

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.370
very quickly, but that's
a little misleading

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:56.600
because the majority of
the weight loss initially

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.970
comes from water loss, not fat loss.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.202
For those of you seeking
long-term weight loss,

00:03:01.202 --> 00:03:04.410
the ketogenic diet is
not super sustainable.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.310
It's graduation day, all
your friends are going to get

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.950
ice cream, some of them are getting

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.506
a cookies and cream milkshakes.

00:03:10.506 --> 00:03:12.970
And you can't have any cause
you on a ketogenic diet,

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:13.803
that's crazy.

00:03:13.803 --> 00:03:15.390
You have to be super vigilant

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.890
when you're on a ketogenic diet

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.620
because carbs have this
nasty habit of just

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.200
sneaking into your foods.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.060
Ketchup, high carb food.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:26.210
Apples, bananas, cookies
and cream milkshakes,

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.290
well, I just love cookies
and cream milkshakes.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.710
And so much for having a
salivatory drink with your friends,

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:32.900
no to alcohol.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.680
Claim number two, the ketogenic
diet is good for the brain.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.800
The truth of the matter is, the
jury's still out on this one

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.910
because science hasn't
given us the answer.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.650
The research on this area just
hasn't been completed yet.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.530
Anecdotally, some people
say they feel more focused

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.670
or sharper when on a ketogenic diet,

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.264
but I've also heard patients
of mine that they feel

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:56.550
foggier, and that Keto Flu
stays with them much longer

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.720
than anticipated.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.389
So I don't like using
anecdotes as reasons why

00:04:00.389 --> 00:04:02.120
a certain diet is good or not.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.350
I need quality research,
which I just don't have.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:08.140
Claim number three, a keto
diet prevents, or manages,

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.640
many chronic diseases.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:13.750
This is a yes and no answer,
where a keto diet really shines

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.910
is in Type II Diabetes.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.510
Because when you have Type II Diabetes,

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:19.690
you have insulin sensitivity issues,

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.680
you have high sugar content in the blood,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.480
and research has shown over and over again

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.882
that the ketogenic diet
for Type II Diabetes works.

00:04:27.882 --> 00:04:28.715
- Yes!

00:04:28.715 --> 00:04:30.860
- We have to talk about Childhood Epilepsy

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.470
because that's where the keto diet

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:33.940
actually got its roots.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.340
We can actually prescribe the
ketogenic diet to children

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.770
who have refractory epileptic seizures,

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.800
and what we find is once they
get into a state of ketosis,

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.290
they have a decreased
frequency of these seizures.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.690
It works, it's proven, it's
evidence-based science.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:51.240
The ketogenic diet has shown some promise

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.770
in the field of oncology, aka cancer.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:57.300
It's not ready to be a prime
time cancer treatment just yet,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.300
and the research doesn't fully support it

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:02.210
to be a preventive measure
for developing cancer.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.830
But what we do know is
that some promises there,

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.923
and more research needs to be done.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.700
Some harms that can stem from
following a ketogenic diet:

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.970
nutritional deficiencies from
cutting out large groups,

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:19.040
and increase in your
"bad" LDL cholesterol,

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.730
kidney issues, bone issues,
and even the increase of

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.790
some certain cancers when
you're overeating foods like

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.360
processed or red meat.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.470
My final thoughts on the keto diet,

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.130
I think it's a good diet for weight loss,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.250
I think it's better for
short-term weight loss

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.270
than long-term weight loss.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.850
So if you have a wedding that
you're getting ready for,

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.910
or some kind of big event that's upcoming,

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.640
and you're otherwise healthy,

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.550
I don't think it's a bad diet to go along.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.480
The fact that the diet is
very difficult to adhere to

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.430
because of how much you
have to drastically change

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:53.250
your eating patterns of the
possible adverse effects

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.270
that can come from following the diet,

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:57.440
and frankly, from the lack of knowledge,

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.386
and the lack of research we
have on its long-term effects,

00:06:00.386 --> 00:06:03.440
all put into question and
really encourage me to

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.480
not recommend this diet to
the majority of my patients

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.470
and to you at home.

